{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/536242-denarian-demons-dresden-files-in-demon-the-descent","id":536242,"title":"Denarian Demons (Dresden Files) in Demon the Descent","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-01T17:14:49-07:00","id":536242,"title":"Denarian Demons (Dresden Files) in Demon the Descent","content":"Greetings all. I have recently been re-reading the Dresden Files and in doing so considered an unusual idea: if one was to create Denarians in DtD, what would they be? <br /> <br /> One of the ideas I've considered is that the coins be a form of infrastructure (for those unaware of the Denarians from the books, they are essentially demons that inhabit the 30 pieces of silver that Judas was given for betraying Jesus). Now, whether the coins were initially designed by the GM to capture and contain powerful demons, or they were re-purposed be demons as an alternative to the existing system of covers I'm not sure. What it would mean is that the demon could possess anyone in possession of their coin, but be unable to create additional covers like a traditional demon.<br /> <br /> Anyone else considered this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3910-lord_salamander","name":"Lord_Salamander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:28:19-07:00","id":536269,"title":"","content":"I haven't considered it but I think you are looking at it from the wrong direction. This is Gm infrastructure, it is (or originally) used by angels possibly to go unnoticed by those who could possibly detect them. Concealment infrastructure that hides an angel within a mortal simply put.On the other note if a demon were to suborn this coin they could use it as the materiel for a gadget (possession) to mimic the angel's use of it.<br /> <br /> If you were to go about using it as a demon trap maybe it radiates extremely strong ethic resonance and when a demon touches it the aether overloads them and forces them to go loud if you want your players to come across it and trigger it. Or if you'd rather it be a plot point than a trap the above extreme aetheric resonance is still present but when a demon touches it a pocket space swallows the demon (acting like a bolthole) so they either release an old prisoner or must save their comrade before someone comes to collect them,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T17:38:13-07:00","id":536278,"title":"","content":"You should check out <b>World of Darkness: Inferno</b>, that book covers a more classical approach to demons and also contains the Possessed (which are ideal for approaching the Denarian-human relationship in the Dresden Files). <br /> <br /> If you wanted to go a step further you could port the demonic form rules over to the Possessed. Tweak the visuals and effects a bit and you've got a pretty spot on denarian port into nWoD with very little system hacking required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T19:22:37-07:00","id":536386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/536242-denarian-demons-dresden-files-in-demon-the-descent?p=536269#post536269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't considered it but I think you are looking at it from the wrong direction. This is Gm infrastructure, it is (or originally) used by angels possibly to go unnoticed by those who could possibly detect them. Concealment infrastructure that hides an angel within a mortal simply put.On the other note if a demon were to suborn this coin they could use it as the materiel for a gadget (possession) to mimic the angel's use of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a really neat idea and makes sense why a demon might take that route rather than build up a series of covers (or in addition to if the demon was really cautious).<br /> <br /> The Possessed is also an interesting take on the idea, and I think I'll have a re-read of those rules and see what I can come up with, thanks! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3910-lord_salamander","name":"Lord_Salamander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T23:01:01-07:00","id":536556,"title":"","content":"Look into flowers of hell, subhoured infrastructure as building materiel for a gadget for even though it may not perfectly line up I feel going that way is safer to retain a sense of balance as well as make it something a pc must work for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T06:53:15-07:00","id":536953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord_Salamander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/536242-denarian-demons-dresden-files-in-demon-the-descent#post536242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings all. I have recently been re-reading the Dresden Files and in doing so considered an unusual idea: if one was to create Denarians in DtD, what would they be?</div> </div> </div> </div> Infernal demon Possessed. <br /> <br /> The problem with doing a direct port is that 1) the denarian demons are flat out evil, drawing power from death and suffering, 2) they can't physically manifest, only possess others (you'd be playing one of the humans possessed), and 3) The demons exist as two-dimensional villains to church's Inquisition and the three Swords - in other words, a Hunter: the Vigil antagonist - instead of being fleshed out personalities on their own. Also, there's 4) the need to somehow turn the Swords into general antagonists of demons, and 5) <br /> <br /> In the WoD, you may play monsters, but you play monsters that struggle with shades of grey. There's no shades of grey with the denarians. There's just no way to paint them as anything remotely approaching PC-material demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you wanted to port them over, I would make the 30 peices of silver into Demon-Form Gadgets that contain the minds of 30 slain demons that can be used by Stigmatics or someone from Heirs to Hell. A denarian game would actually be a game where the main characters are still mortals, not demons themselves. Alternatively, make the denarians into angels instead of the other way around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}